\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Per-control group-level matched satellite-composition contrasts. \(\Delta \) is the matched mean difference in elliptical-vote satellite fraction (CG\textsubscript  {4}{} minus control). The paired sign-flip permutation p-value is primary; the bootstrap p-value is the add-one sign-crossing probability used as a robustness check, with \(B = 9999\) resamples. P-values are not adjusted across the three control definitions; Appendix~\ref {app:pooled_models} reports the Holm sensitivity. The pooled row is secondary. Pair counts: 54 CG\textsubscript  {4}{} groups have complete matching covariates and classified satellites; against Control\textsubscript  {4B}{} and Control\textsubscript  {4C}{} (630 and 632 available control groups) every CG\textsubscript  {4}{} group finds a within-caliper partner, whereas against RG\textsubscript  {4}{} only 52 control groups exist for the 1:1 match without replacement, and the propensity caliper retains 28 pairs on common support.}}{6}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:group_match_per_control}{{3}{6}{Per-control group-level matched satellite-composition contrasts. \(\Delta \) is the matched mean difference in elliptical-vote satellite fraction (\CG {} minus control). The paired sign-flip permutation p-value is primary; the bootstrap p-value is the add-one sign-crossing probability used as a robustness check, with \(B = 9999\) resamples. P-values are not adjusted across the three control definitions; Appendix~\ref {app:pooled_models} reports the Holm sensitivity. The pooled row is secondary. Pair counts: 54 \CG {} groups have complete matching covariates and classified satellites; against \CB {} and \CC {} (630 and 632 available control groups) every \CG {} group finds a within-caliper partner, whereas against \RG {} only 52 control groups exist for the 1:1 match without replacement, and the propensity caliper retains 28 pairs on common support}{table.3}{}}
